ugh experiments with dogs.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ivan-shishman"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ivan-shishman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ivan Shishman</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ivan Shishman was the last tsar of Bulgaria at Tarnovo, reigning from 1371 to 1395.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ivan-sorokin"><span class="enc-name">Ivan Sorokin</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ivan Sorokin was a Kuban Cossack officer and Red commander in the Russian Civil War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ivan-sratsimir"><span class="enc-name">Ivan Sratsimir</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ivan Sratsimir was tsar of Bulgaria at Vidin from 1356 to 1396.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ivan-subasic"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ivan-subasic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ivan Šubašić</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ivan Šubašić was a Croatian politician of the Croatian Peasant Party who served as ban of the autonomous Banovina of Croatia from 1939 to 1941.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ivan-turgenev"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ivan-turgenev.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ivan Turgenev</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ivan Turgenev was a Russian novelist, short story writer, poet, playwright and translator, born in Oryol in 1818 to noble parents, who also made Russian literature…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ivan-vazov"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ivan-vazov.jpg" alt="" loading="laz